WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.140
- All right, let's finish up

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.150
with something awesome
I found on social media.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:04.320
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.320
(rock music)

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.700
If you know me at all,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.770
you know that I'm obsessed
with "The Goonies" movie

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:11.820
since I was a kid.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.653
I love it.

00:00:12.653 --> 00:00:14.850
Ask me anything about the
movie, I probably know it.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:15.900
Where was it shot?

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.980
Mostly Oregon.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.540
Was it Josh Brolin's first movie?

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.952
Yes, it was.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.650
Was that real blood on the treasure map?

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.483
Indeed, it was.

00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.570
I didn't actually know that.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.033
I just read that on the teleprompter.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.150
That's crazy.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.200
And I wanna know that story.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.280
Where did the blood come from?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.180
Who's was it?

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.140
Why was it there?

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:31.973
I don't know.

00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:32.888
These are questions.

00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:35.190
Still though, there's
at least one Goonies fan

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.360
who has got me beat, y'all.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.193
This is incredible.

00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:40.140
In fact, he just dropped
more than $1.6 million

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.340
to buy the actual Goonies
house, which is so cool.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.690
And we have him on the line right now

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.600
at the house in Astoria
watching on Fox 12 Oregon.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.050
What's up, Behman?

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:52.355
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:53.310
(audience clapping)

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.280
- I can't believe you own that house.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.113
That's so cool.

00:00:57.113 --> 00:00:59.730
So, you say your whole life
is connected to "The Goonies."

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.260
How so?

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.400
- Well, after watching the movie

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.780
and seeing this gang of kids

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.150
basically chase One-eyed
Willie's treasure,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.400
it shaped who I am today.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.190
I mean, we used to go as kids
and knock on neighbors houses

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.366
and go down to the basement
looking for tunnels.

00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:14.880
It was awesome.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.230
And so my whole life,

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:18.960
my businesses and
everything that I've set up

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.270
was related to "The Goonies" movie.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.180
I mean, you remember when
they were chasing the treasure

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.741
down in the tunnel, they
found a baseball card.

00:01:26.741 --> 00:01:28.650
Lou Gehrig baseball card.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.415
I buy and sell baseball cards.

00:01:30.415 --> 00:01:32.520
They're chasing golden gems.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.590
I'm in that business as well.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.890
And then how about an escape
room and an ax throwing place?

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.200
I mean, this is all
connected to "The Goonies."

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.480
- Wait, you own an escape room?

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.490
- I have an escape room with four rooms.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.323
I do.

00:01:45.323 --> 00:01:47.040
- Oh my God, I love escape rooms.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.120
That's so cool.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.070
Well, how did you end up with this house

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.020
and are you living in it?

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.087
- Yes, part-time.

00:01:53.087 --> 00:01:54.450
I got super lucky.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.580
I mean, we visited about 10 years ago,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.110
and when we were coming
down the neighborhood

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.510
we're like are we gonna get
arrested for trespassing?

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:01.740
Is this even okay to visit?

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.730
We have no idea.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:05.280
So, I had that feeling
of wouldn't it be amazing

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.830
if we could just walk up
there comfortably and visit?

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.750
Sure enough, my wife
and I were able to go up

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:10.860
and visit the house,

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.870
and we're like we would
love to own this someday

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.866
if that would at all be possible.

00:02:14.866 --> 00:02:17.610
But ever since owning it,

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.090
we got lucky by simply Sandy knowing

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.850
that it was gonna be us that
continued "The Goonies" legacy,

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.290
and so she picked us.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.240
Because we want to recreate this movie

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.940
or this house to look exactly
like it did in the movie,

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.040
including the contraption
in the front yard

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.360
where Chunk did the truffle shuffle.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.193
- Yes.

00:02:34.193 --> 00:02:35.790
- And the inside of the house as well.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.060
So, we just keep telling
Goonies, you're welcome to visit.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.730
Just be respectful to
the neighbors, you know

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.590
just understand it's actually
a neighborhood and whatnot,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.420
but come and visit this iconic house.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.860
You're welcome to come here

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.710
and just know that dreams
really do come true.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.530
- Oh my God, I love you Behman.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.323
This is so cool.

00:02:53.323 --> 00:02:54.600
I love it.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.433
That's so exciting.

00:02:55.433 --> 00:02:56.340
Thank you so much, Behman.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.875
I'm liking your post right now, all right.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.251
(audience clapping)

00:02:59.251 --> 00:03:00.330
- [Behman] Hey you guys.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.120
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.640
- Alright, so usually
this would be the time

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.410
we give our guest $1,000

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.450
courtesy of our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.220
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.720
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.390
but Behman's clearly done
quite well for himself,

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:18.480
'cause he's got 1.6 million
G's to drop on a house.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.950
So, he's fine.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:20.880
He found his treasure.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.970
So, today the money's going
to somebody in the audience.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.634
So, the check
(audience clapping)

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:31.890
is actually under
someone's chair right now.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.060
It's taped to your chair.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.210
Who has it?

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:36.460
(drumroll)

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:41.249
(exciting music)

00:03:44.242 --> 00:03:45.075
Hello.

00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:45.908
What's your name?

00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:46.741
Stand up.

00:03:46.741 --> 00:03:47.574
- Hey.

00:03:47.574 --> 00:03:48.407
- Hi.

00:03:48.407 --> 00:03:49.240
- How are you?

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.073
- What's your name?

00:03:50.073 --> 00:03:50.906
- Ethan.

00:03:50.906 --> 00:03:51.739
- Ethan.
- Yeah.

00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:52.602
- What are you gonna do with a grand?

00:03:52.602 --> 00:03:53.730
- I don't know.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.870
Probably go out for dinner.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:55.770
- All right.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.090
That's a nice dinner, Ethan.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.110
- [Ethan] Yeah.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.070
- Thank you so much.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.450
Hope you have so much fun with it, Ethan.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.950
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:04.380
Keri Russell, O'Shea Jackson, Jr.,

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.730
Justin Hart, and Brynn Cartelli.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.563
Y'all have a great day

00:04:06.563 --> 00:04:08.577
and if it's not, well, try and change it.

